# 03_Journal
## Phase 1: The Journalist
### Chapter 3: Knowing and Knowing Well

Chapter 3 explained why research ethics matters and how researchers should protect the people whose information or behavior they study. This chapter connected to my reasearch project idea about how social media platforms track users interests and use their previous activity to decide what content appears in their feeds. The Facebook emotional-contagion study especially caught my attention because it shows that algorithms do more than simply organize content. By showing some users fewer positive or negative posts, Facebook influenced the emotional tone of what those users later posted. This raised questions about what modern recommendation systems might be doing everyday without users realizing it. 

This chapter made me think more carefully about what makes research ethical. Before reading, I mostly hought research ethics meant completing formas and getting approval before collecting data. However, this historical examples show why so many protections are necessary. 
